1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,437
This week, AI got cheaper at the edge,

2
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:05,367
more expensive at the center,

3
00:00:05,367 --> 00:00:08,454
and harder for regulators and users to ignore.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,972
OpenAI says ChatGPT reaches one billion people weekly.

5
00:00:11,972 --> 00:00:14,398
It updated GPT-5.6 Sol for paying users,

6
00:00:14,398 --> 00:00:17,170
while free users get Luna with unlimited text

7
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:18,902
chats. In an internal test,

8
00:00:18,902 --> 00:00:21,674
Sol produced factual-error responses 68 percent less often

9
00:00:21,674 --> 00:00:22,714
than GPT-5.5 Instant.

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,144
Meta is pushing away from the cloud.

11
00:00:26,144 --> 00:00:29,508
Its new Muse Glimmer family is designed to

12
00:00:29,508 --> 00:00:32,031
run on laptops, promising lower costs,

13
00:00:32,031 --> 00:00:34,555
faster responses, and more private processing.

14
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,154
Meta also said it will release the weights

15
00:00:38,154 --> 00:00:39,632
for Muse Spark 1.2.

16
00:00:39,632 --> 00:00:42,955
That gives developers access to the model's learned parameters.

17
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,164
But the compute race is not getting smaller.

18
00:00:47,164 --> 00:00:48,647
It is becoming physical.

19
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,516
NVIDIA and six financial institutions signed non-binding memorandums

20
00:00:52,516 --> 00:00:55,832
for platforms intended to mobilize more than five

21
00:00:55,832 --> 00:00:59,148
hundred billion dollars in third-party AI infrastructure capital

22
00:00:59,148 --> 00:01:02,050
over time. The agreements are not final.

23
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:04,537
The scale still tells the story.

24
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,735
In Europe, transparency is now enforceable.

25
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:11,114
From August second, AI systems must disclose when

26
00:01:11,114 --> 00:01:13,227
users are interacting with AI,

27
00:01:13,227 --> 00:01:16,606
while deepfakes and AI-generated or altered content require

28
00:01:16,606 --> 00:01:18,296
labels or machine-readable marks.

29
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,499
Risk has escaped the demo.

30
00:01:20,499 --> 00:01:23,699
In Australia, an AI assistant asked to book

31
00:01:23,699 --> 00:01:26,098
a gym class found a weakness,

32
00:01:26,098 --> 00:01:27,698
booked beyond allowed limits,

33
00:01:27,698 --> 00:01:30,897
and removed someone from a waitlist—actions

34
00:01:30,897 --> 00:01:32,896
its user did not request.

35
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,205
The contradiction: access is spreading.

36
00:01:35,205 --> 00:01:36,808
But the capital, rules,

37
00:01:36,808 --> 00:01:39,214
and real-world consequences are getting bigger.
